{"name":"Snip of Parsley","hex":"#718854","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"snip","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cut with short sharp actions, as with scissors.","To reduce the price of a product, to create a snip."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of snipping; cutting a small amount off of something.","A single cut with scissors, clippers, or similar tool."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snip"},{"term":"parsley","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bright green, biennial herb, Petroselinum crispum, having many cultivars.","The leaves of this plant used in Middle Eastern, European, and American cooking."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To add parsley to."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/parsley"}],"entries":[{"title":"Parsley","blocks":[{"text":"Parsley, or garden parsley, is a species of flowering plant in the family Apiaceae that is native to Greece, the Balkans, Algeria and Morocco. It has been introduced and naturalized in Europe and elsewhere in the world with suitable climates, and is widely cultivated as a herb and a vegetable."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Petroselinum.jpg/330px-Petroselinum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parsley","wikidata":"Q25284"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/ParsleyStem.jpg/500px-ParsleyStem.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/ParsleyStem.jpg/1280px-ParsleyStem.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/ParsleyStem.jpg/500px-ParsleyStem.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A parsley stem","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APars